-- title:
--   Ordinary line at p when p ∥ M and θ(Uₚ) ≠ 0
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime, $M \geq 1$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^{2} \nmid M$, let $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$ be finite with $p \notin S$, and let $F$ be a field of characteristic $p$. Write $\mathbb{T}$ for `heckeAlgebra M 2 S`, the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$, together with the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M$, $q \notin S$. Let $\theta \colon \mathbb{T} \to F$ be a ring homomorphism with $\theta(U_p) \neq 0$, and let $\rho \colon \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ be a group homomorphism such that: $\rho$ is trivial on the pointwise stabiliser of some intermediate field $L$ with $[L:\mathbb{Q}]$ finite; for every $u \in F^{2}$, $u \neq 0$, some $\rho(\sigma)$ moves $u$ out of $F\!\cdot\!u$; and for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and inducing $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, one has $\mathrm{tr}\,\rho(\sigma) = \theta(T_\ell)$ and $\det \rho(\sigma) = \ell$ in $F$. Let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ having $p$ as a non-unit. Then there is $v \in F^{2}$, $v \neq 0$, such that: $\rho(\sigma) v \in F\!\cdot\!v$ for all $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $P$; $\rho(\sigma) w - w \in F\!\cdot\!v$ for every $w \in F^{2}$ and every $\sigma$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of $P$; $\rho(\sigma) w - \theta(U_p)\, w \in F\!\cdot\!v$ for every $w$ and every $\sigma$ acting as $x \mapsto x^{p}$ on the residue field of $P$ from the decomposition subgroup; and $\rho(\sigma) v = a \cdot v$ whenever $\sigma$ lies in the image of the inertia subgroup and $a \in \mathbb{N}$ satisfies $\sigma\mu = \mu^{a}$ for all $\mu \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\mu^{p} = 1$.
--
--   This is the local description at $p$, in transport form, of a mod $p$ representation attached to a weight-two eigensystem of level $M$ with $p \parallel M$ and non-zero $U_p$-eigenvalue: the representation restricted to the decomposition group at $p$ is reducible, upper triangular with unramified quotient on which Frobenius acts by $\theta(U_p)$, and with the cyclotomic character on the stable line. It is stated for an arbitrary irreducible finite-level $\rho$ with the prescribed Frobenius traces and determinants, and is used in [`GaloisRep.exists_stableLine_of_theta_T_ne_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_three_le_of_eq_three`](thm.html#GaloisRep.exists_stableLine_of_theta_T_ne_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_three_le_of_eq_three).
